sn21.6:2.1 starts: “Geese, herons, and peacocks,
sn21.6:2.2 starts: Elephants, and spotted deer,
sn21.6:2.3 starts: All are frightened of the lion
sn21.6:2.4 starts: Regardless of their bodies’ size.
sn22.78:3.1 starts: “When the Buddha, through direct knowledge,
sn22.78:3.2 starts: Sets in motion the Wheel of Dhamma,
sn22.78:3.3 starts: The peerless Teacher in this world
sn22.78:3.4 starts: With its devas makes this known:
sn22.95:14.1 starts: “A bhikkhu with energy aroused
sn22.95:14.2 starts: Should look upon the aggregates thus,
sn22.95:14.3 starts: Whether by day or at night,
sn22.95:14.4 starts: Comprehending, ever mindful.
sn35.132:3.1 starts: They took delight in Dhamma and meditation,
sn35.132:3.2 starts: Those brahmins who recalled the ancient rules.
sn35.136:3.1 starts: “These are considered happiness
sn35.136:3.2 starts: By the world with its devas;
sn35.136:3.3 starts: But where these cease,
sn35.136:3.4 starts: That they consider suffering.
sn35.136:7.1 starts: “But for the good it is disclosed,
sn35.136:7.2 starts: It is light here for those who see.
sn35.136:7.3 starts: The dullards unskilled in the Dhamma
sn35.136:7.4 starts: Don’t understand it in its presence.
sn35.136:8.1 starts: “This Dhamma isn’t easily understood
sn35.136:8.2 starts: By those afflicted with lust for existence,
sn35.136:8.3 starts: Who flow along in the stream of existence,
sn35.136:8.4 starts: Deeply mired in Mara’s realm.
